stimuli.content:
In a certain code language:
'A lo B' means 'A is the mother of B';
'A pa B' means 'A is the brother of B';
'A ki B' means 'A is the husband of B';
'A su B' means 'A is the daughter of B';
'A ne B' means 'A is the sister of B'.
In every expression, a married couple's children are the children of both spouses.

questions.question_text:
In a certain code:
'A $ B' means 'A is the son of B';
'A % B' means 'A is the wife of B';
'A @ B' means 'A is the sister of B';
'A # B' means 'A is the father of B';
'A & B' means 'A is the mother of B'.

If 'K & L @ M % N $ O', which of the following is definitely true?
